  "discussion": "For non-volatile flash memory media, a technique known as wear levelling ensures that writes are distributed evenly across each memory block. This feature necessitates non-volatile flash memory media being overwritten with a random pattern at least twice, and followed by a read back for verification, as this helps to ensure that all memory blocks are overwritten.",
